55
00:03:30.441 --> 00:03:32.105
Solve it with Spring Boot 4.

56
00:03:33.355 --> 00:03:46.261
A coordinator fans out every request to N replica services over HTTP with RestClient, on virtual threads, and answers as soon as W writes or R reads succeed within the timeout.

57
00:03:46.541 --> 00:03:50.424
Reads return the newest version and read-repair stale replicas.

58
00:03:50.704 --> 00:03:58.469
In the test, the replicas are real HTTP endpoints that can be taken down, so failures behave like separate nodes.

